एक + -अन्नम् + .({@-न्नः@}), {@-˚आदिन्@}
—1 a mess-mate.
—2 One who lives on the alms from only one house; नैकान्नादी भवेद् व्रती Ms. 2. 188.

एक + -अन्नम् + .({@-न्नः@}), {@-˚आदिन्@}
—1 a mess-mate.
—2 One who lives on the alms from only one house; नैकान्नादी भवेद् व्रती Ms. 2. 188.

एक + -आतपत्र a. characterized by only one umbrella (showing universal
 sovereignty); एकातपत्रं जगतः प्रभुत्वम् R. 2. 47. ˚त्रां भुवम् 18. 4;
 K. 206; Śi. 12. 33; V. 3. 19.

एक + -आदेशः cf. Sk. on P. VI. 1. 101 one substitute for two or more
 letters (got by either dropping one vowel, or by the blending of both);
 as the आ in एकायन.

एक + -कालीन a.
—1 happening once only;
—2 Contemporary, coeval.

एक + -कुण्डलः, -कुण्डलिन्, N. of Kubera; of Balabhadra and Śeṣa;
 गर्गस्रोतो महातीर्थमाजगामैककुण्डली Mb. 9. 37. 14. cf. एककुण्डल
 आख्यातो बलरामे धनाधिपे Med.

एक + -कुण्डलः, -कुण्डलिन्, N. of Kubera; of Balabhadra and Śeṣa;
 गर्गस्रोतो महातीर्थमाजगामैककुण्डली Mb. 9. 37. 14. cf. एककुण्डल
 आख्यातो बलरामे धनाधिपे Med.

एक + -जातीय a. of the same kind, species or family. {@˚अनुसमयः@}
 performance of one detail with reference to all things or persons, then
 doing the second, then the third and so on (see पदार्थानुसमय) Ms. 5. 2. 1-2.

एकादश + .{@-शी@}
—1 The eleventh day of every fortnight of a lunar month, sacred to Viṣṇu;
 (when fasting is enjoined and is considered to be productive of great
 religious merit).
—2 Presentations of offerings to deceased ancestors or Pitṛs on the eleventh
 day after decease.
